IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-time`
IMPORT `wa-interpretation-part6`

-- Tests for the constituents of the section 45A(4) lists (wa-interpretation-part6.l4).  Pass 1 had one constructor per printed list;
-- pass 2 added one per constituent, so "permit" alone or "renew" alone is answered.  The bundles still answer TRUE.

§ `Tests -- section 45A(4) constituents`

-- src:543 | (4) In this section —
-- src:544 | fee includes charge;
-- src:545 | issue includes grant, give or renew;
-- src:546 | licence includes registration, right, permit, authority, approval or exemption.
@ref s 45A(4) (src:543-546)
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `to grant, for the word issue` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `to give, for the word issue` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `to renew, for the word issue` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `a registration, for the word licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `a right, for the word licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `a permit, for the word licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `an authority, for the word licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `an approval, for the word licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `an exemption, for the word licence` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `a charge, for the word fee` EQUALS JUST TRUE
#ASSERT `it is within the meaning of the word in section 45A` `something else` EQUALS NOTHING
